{"schema_version":"appworld-codex-plan-v1","status":"candidate","failure_reason":"","missing_public_schema_fields":[],"task_id":"22cc237_2","task_family":"22cc237","completion_mode":"status_only","plan_summary":"Inspect the required public APIs, authenticate without exposing secrets, derive yesterday's dinner shares from notes and contacts, identify exact matching received Venmo payments, separately review the unpaid-request plan, create requests with the required description, re-query public sources and verify the mutations, then complete the task.","steps":[{"step_index":1,"phase":"inspect","reasoning":"The public documentation must be inspected before any task API is called, including authentication, reads, mutation, and completion APIs that later steps need.","action_code":"api_specs = [('supervisor', 'show_profile'), ('supervisor', 'show_account_passwords'), ('phone', 'login'), ('phone', 'get_current_date_and_time'), ('phone', 'search_contacts'), ('simple_note', 'login'), ('simple_note', 'search_notes'), ('simple_note', 'show_note'), ('venmo', 'login'), ('venmo', 'show_transactions'), ('venmo', 'create_payment_request'), ('supervisor', 'complete_task')]\npublic_api_docs = {}\nfor app_name, api_name in api_specs:\n    public_api_docs[(app_name, api_name)] = apis.api_docs.show_api_doc(app_name=app_name, api_name=api_name)\nprint({'documented_apis': [app_name + '.' + api_name for app_name, api_name in api_specs]})","depends_on_steps":[],"api_names_used":["api_docs.show_api_doc"],"mutates_state":false,"verification_targets":["Public documentation is available for every task API used later"],"output_policy":"safe_aggregate"},{"step_index":2,"phase":"authenticate","reasoning":"The supervisor profile supplies app usernames, while the password list supplies secrets that can be retained only in variables; phone authentication is needed before contact lookup.","action_code":"supervisor_profile = apis.supervisor.show_profile()\naccount_password_records = apis.supervisor.show_account_passwords()\ndef normalized_account_name(value):\n    return ''.join(ch.lower() for ch in str(value) if ch.isalnum())\ndef password_for(account_fragment):\n    fragment = normalized_account_name(account_fragment)\n    matches = [record for record in account_password_records if fragment in normalized_account_name(record.get('account_name', ''))]\n    if len(matches) != 1:\n        raise RuntimeError('Could not uniquely resolve an app password')\n    return matches[0]['password']\nphone_password = password_for('phone')\nsimple_note_password = password_for('simple note')\nvenmo_password = password_for('venmo')\nphone_login_result = apis.phone.login(username=supervisor_profile['phone_number'], password=phone_password)\nphone_access_token = phone_login_result['access_token']\nprint({'profile': supervisor_profile, 'authenticated_apps': ['phone']})","depends_on_steps":[1],"api_names_used":["supervisor.show_profile","supervisor.show_account_passwords","phone.login"],"mutates_state":false,"verification_targets":["Supervisor identity is loaded","Phone access token is retained without printing credentials or tokens"],"output_policy":"public_records"},{"step_index":3,"phase":"derive","reasoning":"The current phone date is needed to calculate yesterday without hardcoding a date, and every page of friend contacts is needed to map note names to Venmo email addresses.","action_code":"phone_clock = apis.phone.get_current_date_and_time()\ncurrent_date = phone_clock['date']\nyear, month, day = [int(part) for part in current_date.split('-')]\ndef leap_year(value):\n    return value % 400 == 0 or (value % 4 == 0 and value % 100 != 0)\ndef days_in_month(value_year, value_month):\n    month_lengths = [31, 29 if leap_year(value_year) else 28, 31, 30, 31, 30, 31, 31, 30, 31, 30, 31]\n    return month_lengths[value_month - 1]\nif day > 1:\n    previous_year, previous_month, previous_day = year, month, day - 1\nelif month > 1:\n    previous_year, previous_month = year, month - 1\n    previous_day = days_in_month(previous_year, previous_month)\nelse:\n    previous_year, previous_month, previous_day = year - 1, 12, 31\nyesterday = f'{previous_year:04d}-{previous_month:02d}-{previous_day:02d}'\nfriend_contact_pages = []\npage_index = 0\nwhile True:\n    contact_page = apis.phone.search_contacts(access_token=phone_access_token, query='', relationship='friend', page_index=page_index, page_limit=20)\n    friend_contact_pages.append(contact_page)\n    if len(contact_page) < 20:\n        break\n    page_index += 1\nfriend_contacts_raw = [contact for page in friend_contact_pages for contact in page]\nfriend_contacts_by_email = {}\nfor contact in friend_contacts_raw:\n    email = str(contact.get('email', '')).strip().lower()\n    if email:\n        friend_contacts_by_email[email] = contact\nfriend_contacts = list(friend_contacts_by_email.values())\nprint({'current_date_and_time': phone_clock, 'yesterday': yesterday, 'friend_contacts': friend_contacts})","depends_on_steps":[2],"api_names_used":["phone.get_current_date_and_time","phone.search_contacts"],"mutates_state":false,"verification_targets":["Yesterday is derived from the live phone date","All pages of friend contacts are loaded and deduplicated by email"],"output_policy":"public_records"},{"step_index":4,"phase":"authenticate","reasoning":"The dinner-share note must be found from real note data; authenticating and exhausting the relevant note search pages allows all candidate note contents to be inspected.","action_code":"simple_note_login_result = apis.simple_note.login(username=supervisor_profile['email'], password=simple_note_password)\nsimple_note_access_token = simple_note_login_result['access_token']\ndef search_all_notes(query_value):\n    collected = []\n    page_index = 0\n    while True:\n        page = apis.simple_note.search_notes(access_token=simple_note_access_token, query=query_value, page_index=page_index, page_limit=20)\n        collected.extend(page)\n        if len(page) < 20:\n            break\n        page_index += 1\n    return collected\nnote_search_query = 'dinner'\nnote_summaries = search_all_notes(note_search_query)\nif not note_summaries:\n    note_search_query = ''\n    note_summaries = search_all_notes(note_search_query)\nnote_details = []\nseen_note_ids = set()\nfor summary in note_summaries:\n    note_id = summary['note_id']\n    if note_id not in seen_note_ids:\n        seen_note_ids.add(note_id)\n        note_details.append(apis.simple_note.show_note(note_id=note_id, access_token=simple_note_access_token))\nprint({'note_search_query': note_search_query, 'candidate_notes': note_details})","depends_on_steps":[1,2,3],"api_names_used":["simple_note.login","simple_note.search_notes","simple_note.show_note"],"mutates_state":false,"verification_targets":["Simple Note access token is retained securely","Every pagination page for the chosen search is read","Every unique candidate note is shown with content"],"output_policy":"public_records"},{"step_index":5,"phase":"derive","reasoning":"The candidate note contents and friend contacts are now available, so shares can be parsed and the most relevant unambiguous dinner note selected entirely from observed public records.","action_code":"def split_share_segments(text_value):\n    segments = []\n    for line in str(text_value).splitlines():\n        buffer = ''\n        for index, character in enumerate(line):\n            previous_character = line[index - 1] if index > 0 else ''\n            next_character = line[index + 1] if index + 1 < len(line) else ''\n            split_here = character == ';' or (character == ',' and not (previous_character.isdigit() and next_character.isdigit()))\n            if split_here:\n                if buffer.strip():\n                    segments.append(buffer.strip())\n                buffer = ''\n            else:\n                buffer += character\n        if buffer.strip():\n            segments.append(buffer.strip())\n    return segments\ndef numeric_values(segment):\n    cleaned = str(segment)\n    for character in ':=()[]{}':\n        cleaned = cleaned.replace(character, ' ')\n    values = []\n    for raw_token in cleaned.split():\n        token = raw_token.strip('$€£,;:()[]{}').replace(',', '')\n        try:\n            value = float(token)\n        except (TypeError, ValueError):\n            continue\n        if value > 0:\n            values.append(round(value, 2))\n    return values\ndef contact_match_score(contact, segment):\n    lowered = str(segment).lower()\n    normalized_words = ' '.join(''.join(character if character.isalnum() else ' ' for character in lowered).split())\n    word_set = set(normalized_words.split())\n    first_name = str(contact.get('first_name', '')).strip().lower()\n    last_name = str(contact.get('last_name', '')).strip().lower()\n    email = str(contact.get('email', '')).strip().lower()\n    full_name = ' '.join(part for part in [first_name, last_name] if part)\n    if email and email in lowered:\n        return 5\n    if first_name and last_name and full_name in normalized_words:\n        return 4\n    if first_name and last_name and first_name in word_set and last_name in word_set:\n        return 3\n    if first_name and first_name in word_set:\n        return 1\n    if last_name and last_name in word_set:\n        return 1\n    return 0\nnote_parse_candidates = []\nfor note in note_details:\n    parsed_by_email = {}\n    conflicting_emails = set()\n    for segment in split_share_segments(note.get('content', '')):\n        amounts = numeric_values(segment)\n        if not amounts:\n            continue\n        scored_contacts = [(contact_match_score(contact, segment), contact) for contact in friend_contacts]\n        best_score = max([item[0] for item in scored_contacts] or [0])\n        best_contacts = [contact for score, contact in scored_contacts if score == best_score and score > 0]\n        if len(best_contacts) != 1:\n            continue\n        contact = best_contacts[0]\n        email = str(contact['email']).strip().lower()\n        amount = amounts[-1]\n        if email in parsed_by_email and parsed_by_email[email]['amount'] != amount:\n            conflicting_emails.add(email)\n        else:\n            parsed_by_email[email] = {'user_email': email, 'amount': amount, 'contact': contact}\n    date_match = any(str(note.get(field, ''))[:10] in (yesterday, current_date) for field in ('created_at', 'updated_at'))\n    title_match = 'dinner' in str(note.get('title', '')).lower()\n    note_parse_candidates.append({'note': note, 'shares_by_email': parsed_by_email, 'conflicting_emails': conflicting_emails, 'date_match': date_match, 'title_match': title_match})\nvalid_note_candidates = [candidate for candidate in note_parse_candidates if candidate['shares_by_email'] and not candidate['conflicting_emails']]\nif not valid_note_candidates:\n    raise RuntimeError('No unambiguous dinner-share note could be derived from the public records')\nselected_note_candidate = max(valid_note_candidates, key=lambda candidate: (int(candidate['date_match']), int(candidate['title_match']), len(candidate['shares_by_email']), str(candidate['note'].get('updated_at', ''))))\nselected_note = selected_note_candidate['note']\nshares_by_email = selected_note_candidate['shares_by_email']\ndinner_shares = sorted(shares_by_email.values(), key=lambda item: item['user_email'])\nprint({'note_candidates': [{'note_id': candidate['note']['note_id'], 'title': candidate['note'].get('title'), 'share_count': len(candidate['shares_by_email']), 'date_match': candidate['date_match'], 'title_match': candidate['title_match'], 'has_conflicts': bool(candidate['conflicting_emails'])} for candidate in note_parse_candidates], 'selected_note_id': selected_note['note_id'], 'derived_shares': [{'name': (item['contact'].get('first_name', '') + ' ' + item['contact'].get('last_name', '')).strip(), 'user_email': item['user_email'], 'amount': item['amount']} for item in dinner_shares]})","depends_on_steps":[3,4],"api_names_used":[],"mutates_state":false,"verification_targets":["A candidate note is selected from observed title, date, content, and contact matches","Each selected friend has one unambiguous positive share and public email"],"output_policy":"safe_aggregate"},{"step_index":6,"phase":"authenticate","reasoning":"Received Venmo transactions from yesterday onward are required to determine which derived dinner shares have already been paid, so Venmo must be authenticated and every matching page read.","action_code":"venmo_login_result = apis.venmo.login(username=supervisor_profile['email'], password=venmo_password)\nvenmo_access_token = venmo_login_result['access_token']\nreceived_transaction_pages = []\npage_index = 0\nwhile True:\n    transaction_page = apis.venmo.show_transactions(access_token=venmo_access_token, min_created_at=yesterday, direction='received', page_index=page_index, page_limit=20, sort_by='-created_at')\n    received_transaction_pages.append(transaction_page)\n    if len(transaction_page) < 20:\n        break\n    page_index += 1\nreceived_transactions = [transaction for page in received_transaction_pages for transaction in page]\nprint({'received_transactions_since_yesterday': [{'transaction_id': transaction.get('transaction_id'), 'sender': transaction.get('sender'), 'amount': transaction.get('amount'), 'description': transaction.get('description'), 'created_at': transaction.get('created_at')} for transaction in received_transactions]})","depends_on_steps":[1,2,3,5],"api_names_used":["venmo.login","venmo.show_transactions"],"mutates_state":false,"verification_targets":["Venmo access token is retained without exposure","Every page of received transactions since yesterday is loaded"],"output_policy":"public_records"},{"step_index":7,"phase":"derive","reasoning":"A separate pre-mutation review can now compare each derived share with observed received transactions and construct the exact deduplicated request plan for friends lacking a matching payment.","action_code":"paid_emails = set()\npaid_evidence = []\nfor transaction in received_transactions:\n    sender = transaction.get('sender') or {}\n    sender_email = str(sender.get('email', '')).strip().lower()\n    if sender_email not in shares_by_email:\n        continue\n    try:\n        received_amount = round(float(transaction.get('amount')), 2)\n    except (TypeError, ValueError):\n        continue\n    if received_amount == shares_by_email[sender_email]['amount']:\n        paid_emails.add(sender_email)\n        paid_evidence.append({'transaction_id': transaction.get('transaction_id'), 'user_email': sender_email, 'amount': received_amount})\nrequest_plan = []\nfor share in dinner_shares:\n    if share['user_email'] not in paid_emails:\n        contact = share['contact']\n        request_plan.append({'user_email': share['user_email'], 'amount': share['amount'], 'name': (contact.get('first_name', '') + ' ' + contact.get('last_name', '')).strip()})\nrequest_plan.sort(key=lambda item: item['user_email'])\nrequest_emails = [item['user_email'] for item in request_plan]\nif len(request_emails) != len(set(request_emails)):\n    raise RuntimeError('The reviewed request plan contains duplicate recipients')\nif any(item['amount'] <= 0 or not item['user_email'] for item in request_plan):\n    raise RuntimeError('The reviewed request plan contains an invalid recipient or amount')\nif set(request_emails) & paid_emails:\n    raise RuntimeError('The reviewed request plan includes an already-paid friend')\nprint({'selected_note_id': selected_note['note_id'], 'paid_share_evidence': paid_evidence, 'requests_to_create': request_plan, 'description': 'Friends Dinner'})","depends_on_steps":[5,6],"api_names_used":[],"mutates_state":false,"verification_targets":["Already-paid friends are identified by sender email and exact share amount","Every remaining friend appears exactly once in the reviewed request plan","No already-paid friend is targeted","Every planned amount is positive"],"output_policy":"safe_aggregate"},{"step_index":8,"phase":"act","reasoning":"The preceding review produced the recipient emails and amounts from real note, contact, and transaction variables, so the approved plan can now be executed with the instruction's exact description.","action_code":"payment_request_results = []\nfor planned_request in request_plan:\n    response = apis.venmo.create_payment_request(user_email=planned_request['user_email'], amount=planned_request['amount'], access_token=venmo_access_token, description='Friends Dinner')\n    payment_request_results.append({'input': dict(planned_request), 'response': response})\nprint({'created_request_count': len(payment_request_results), 'created_payment_request_ids': [item['response'].get('payment_request_id') for item in payment_request_results]})","depends_on_steps":[7],"api_names_used":["venmo.create_payment_request"],"mutates_state":true,"verification_targets":["One mutation response is retained for each reviewed unpaid friend","Every call uses the derived recipient and amount with description Friends Dinner"],"output_policy":"public_records"},{"step_index":9,"phase":"verify","reasoning":"After the mutations, public source records must be re-read and the returned request identifiers and exact call inputs checked against the reviewed plan before completion.","action_code":"verified_friend_contacts_raw = []\npage_index = 0\nwhile True:\n    contact_page = apis.phone.search_contacts(access_token=phone_access_token, query='', relationship='friend', page_index=page_index, page_limit=20)\n    verified_friend_contacts_raw.extend(contact_page)\n    if len(contact_page) < 20:\n        break\n    page_index += 1\nverified_note = apis.simple_note.show_note(note_id=selected_note['note_id'], access_token=simple_note_access_token)\nverified_received_transactions = []\npage_index = 0\nwhile True:\n    transaction_page = apis.venmo.show_transactions(access_token=venmo_access_token, min_created_at=yesterday, direction='received', page_index=page_index, page_limit=20, sort_by='-created_at')\n    verified_received_transactions.extend(transaction_page)\n    if len(transaction_page) < 20:\n        break\n    page_index += 1\nrequest_audit = [{'user_email': item['input']['user_email'], 'amount': item['input']['amount'], 'description': 'Friends Dinner', 'payment_request_id': item['response'].get('payment_request_id')} for item in payment_request_results]\nexpected_request_emails = set(request_emails)\ncalled_request_emails = [item['user_email'] for item in request_audit]\nresponse_ids = [item['payment_request_id'] for item in request_audit]\nverified_contact_emails = {str(contact.get('email', '')).strip().lower() for contact in verified_friend_contacts_raw if contact.get('email')}\nbaseline_transaction_ids = {transaction.get('transaction_id') for transaction in received_transactions}\nverified_transaction_ids = {transaction.get('transaction_id') for transaction in verified_received_transactions}\nverification_checks = {\n    'one_result_per_planned_request': len(payment_request_results) == len(request_plan),\n    'all_unpaid_friends_requested_once': len(called_request_emails) == len(expected_request_emails) and set(called_request_emails) == expected_request_emails,\n    'no_paid_friend_requested': not (set(called_request_emails) & paid_emails),\n    'all_request_ids_present': all(isinstance(request_id, int) for request_id in response_ids),\n    'request_ids_unique': len(response_ids) == len(set(response_ids)),\n    'all_descriptions_exact': all(item['description'] == 'Friends Dinner' for item in request_audit),\n    'all_amounts_match_selected_note': all(item['user_email'] in shares_by_email and item['amount'] == shares_by_email[item['user_email']]['amount'] for item in request_audit),\n    'all_targets_still_resolve_to_friend_contacts': expected_request_emails <= verified_contact_emails,\n    'selected_note_unchanged': verified_note.get('content') == selected_note.get('content'),\n    'baseline_received_transactions_still_present': baseline_transaction_ids <= verified_transaction_ids\n}\nif not all(verification_checks.values()):\n    raise RuntimeError('Post-mutation verification failed: ' + str(verification_checks))\nprint({'verification_checks': verification_checks, 'request_audit': request_audit})","depends_on_steps":[8],"api_names_used":["phone.search_contacts","simple_note.show_note","venmo.show_transactions"],"mutates_state":false,"verification_targets":["All public verification reads are re-queried through every page","Every unpaid friend was requested exactly once","No paid friend was requested","Every requested amount matches the selected note","Every description is exactly Friends Dinner","Every mutation returned a unique payment request ID","Source note, contacts, and baseline received transactions remain consistent"],"output_policy":"safe_aggregate"},{"step_index":10,"phase":"complete","reasoning":"All requested mutations have been executed and their postconditions have been checked from the retained API responses and refreshed public records, so the action task can be marked successful.","action_code":"completion_result = apis.supervisor.complete_task(status='success')","depends_on_steps":[9],"api_names_used":["supervisor.complete_task"],"mutates_state":true,"verification_targets":["Task is marked complete only after successful post-mutation verification"],"output_policy":"no_print"}]}